<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4651" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλουργ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς, ἔργον</span>) lit. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wrought in</i> or <i>by the sea,</i> always
			in sense <i>sea-purple,</i> i.e. <i>genuine purple dye,</i> opp.
			imitations, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβαίνονθ᾽
			ἁλουργέσιν</span> on <i>cloths of purple,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				946
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίτρα ἁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					100
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρώμαθ᾽ ἁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					41.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					110c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Col.</u>
					792a7
				</span></i>
			:—less freq. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλουργός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span> (also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				41
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					429d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιτωνίσκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.754.12
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				14
			</span></i>, etc. (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἁλουργής</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				21
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στολαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phylarch.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωμναί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				81
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλουργοῦς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.757
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				442a24
			</span></i>, 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλοργοῦς</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5702.23
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Samos</span>).</div>
